2437,Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2437 Arabic Hadees: 2594
2438,"On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""I saw in a dream last night a canopy dripping with ghee and honey, and I saw people scooping from it—some taking much, some taking little. And there was a rope extending from the earth to the heaven. I saw you grasp it and ascend; then another man grasped it and ascended; then another man grasped it and ascended; then another man grasped it and it was severed, then it was rejoined for him and he ascended.""Abū Bakr said: ""O Messenger of Allah! May my father and mother be ransomed for you—allow me to interpret it."" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Interpret it."" He said: ""As for the canopy, it is Islam. As for that which drips of honey and ghee, it is the Qurʾān—its sweetness drips—so the one who takes much of the Qurʾān and the one who takes little. As for the rope extending from the heaven to the earth, it is the Truth upon which you are; you grasp it and Allah raises you, then a man grasps it and rises, then another man grasps it and rises, then another man grasps it and it is severed for him, then it is rejoined for him and he rises."" He said: ""Inform me, O Messenger of Allah! May my father and mother be ransomed for you—did I get it right or err?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""You got some right and you erred in some."" He said: ""By Allah, you must tell me what I erred in."" He said: ""Do not swear."""
