2464,"Jabir ibn Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Narrate from the Children of Israel, and there is no harm in that, for there were wonders among them."" Then he began to narrate and said: ""A group from the Children of Israel went out until they came to one of their graveyards. They said: 'Let us pray two rak'ahs and supplicate to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, that He brings out for us a man from among those who have died, so we may ask him about death.' He said: So they did that. While they were in that state, a man peered his head out from a grave among those graves. He was dark-skinned, with the mark of prostration between his eyes. He said: 'O you people, what do you want from me? I have been dead for a hundred years, and the heat of death has not subsided from me until now. So supplicate to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for me that He returns me as I was.'"""
