2472,"On the authority of Ibn al-Adra', who said: I was guarding the Prophet ﷺ one night when he went out to relieve himself. He saw me, took my hand, and we walked on. We passed by a man praying and reciting the Qur'an aloud. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Perhaps he is showing off."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, he is reciting the Qur'an aloud."" He withdrew his hand and said: ""You will not attain this matter by force."" Then on another night, he went out while I was guarding him to relieve himself. He took my hand and we passed by a man praying with the Qur'an. I said: ""Perhaps he is showing off."" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""No, indeed he is one who turns to Allah often in repentance."" I looked, and behold, it was Abdullah Dhu al-Najadayn."
2473,Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2473 Arabic Hadees: 748
2474,"On the authority of Al-'Irbad ibn Sariyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gave us an admonition that made the eyes shed tears and the hearts tremble with fear. So we said: ""O Messenger of Allah! This is indeed the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us?"" He said: ""I have left you upon the clear path, its night like its day; no one deviates from it after me except one who is doomed. And whoever among you lives long will see much difference. So hold fast to what you know of my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs after me; cling to it with your molar teeth. And adhere to obedience, even if it be to an Abyssinian slave. For the believer is like a submissive camel; wherever it is led, it follows."""
