2493,"On the authority of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Safwan ibn 'Assal al-Muradi narrated, saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) while he was reclining in the mosque on a red cloak of his. I said to him: O Messenger of Allah! I have come seeking knowledge. He said: Welcome to the seeker of knowledge! Indeed, the seeker of knowledge is surrounded by angels who shade him with their wings, then they stack upon one another until they reach the lowest heaven, out of love for what he seeks. Safwan said: O Messenger of Allah! We still travel between Mecca and Medina, so give us a ruling on wiping over the leather socks? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Three days for the traveler, and one day and one night for the resident."
