2505,"Hudhayfah ibn al-Yamān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) about the good, but I used to ask him about the evil out of fear that it might reach me. So I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We were in ignorance and evil, then Allah brought us this good (and we are in it), (and He brought you), so is there any evil after this good (as there was before it)?"" (He said: ""O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah and follow what is in it,"" (three times). He said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there any good after this evil?"") He said: ""Yes."" (I said: ""Then what is the protection from it?"" He said: ""The sword."") I said: ""And is there any evil after that good?"" (And in a narration: I said: ""And is there any remainder after the sword?"") He said: ""Yes, and in it (and in a narration: there will be an emirate (and in a wording: a group) on spears, and a truce on) smoke."" I said: ""And what is its smoke?"" He said: ""A people (and in another narration: there will be after me imams (who follow other than my Sunnah, and) they guide with other than my guidance, you recognize from them and you deny (and there will arise among them men whose hearts are the hearts of devils in bodies of humans). (And in another: The truce on smoke, what is it? He said: The hearts of a people do not return to what they were upon)."" I said: ""Then is there any evil after that good?"" He said: ""Yes, (a blind and deaf fitnah upon it) are callers at the gates of Hell, whoever answers them to it they will throw him into it."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Describe them to us."" He said: ""They are from our skin and they speak with our tongues."" I said: ""(O Messenger of Allah!) Then what do you command me if that reaches me?"" He said: ""You adhere to the Jamāʿah of the Muslims and their Imām, (you listen and obey the Amīr even if your back is struck and your wealth is taken, so listen and obey)."" I said: ""What if they have no Jamāʿah and no Imām?"" He said: ""Then withdraw from all those sects entirely, even if you have to bite onto the root of a tree until death reaches you while you are upon that."" (And in a narration): ""So if you die, O Hudhayfah, while you are biting onto a stump, it is better for you than following any one of them."" (And in another): ""So if you see on that day Allah — Mighty and Majestic — on the earth a Caliph, then adhere to him even if your back is struck and your wealth is taken; but if you do not see a Caliph, then flee (in the earth) until death reaches you while you are biting onto the root of a tree."" (He said: I said: ""Then what?"" He said: ""Then the Dajjāl emerges."" I said: ""Then with what does he come?"" He said: ""With a river — or he said: water and fire — so whoever enters his river, his reward is nullified and his sin is obligated, and whoever enters his fire, his reward is obligated and his sin is nullified."" (I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Then what is after the Dajjāl?"" He said: ""Jesus son of Mary""). He said: I said: ""Then what?"" He said: ""If you were to breed a horse, you would not ride its foal until the Hour is established."""
2506,Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 2506 Arabic Hadees: 2868
